<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monnet Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Monnet Plan was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s first plan for reconstruction and modernisation, drawn up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-monnet">Jean Monnet</a>'s planning commission and adopted in 1946. It directed investment to basic industries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a>, electricity, cement, farm machinery and transport, and was partly financed by Marshall aid. It set the model of indicative planning that guided French economic growth in the following decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monnet-plan.jpg" alt="Monnet Plan" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author (Keystone France) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Monnet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
